From c0d125bbcf8fe2fabc08b2fdcefac3088bc83147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Blackfold (Grok Bot for Aaron)" <blackfold@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:59:29 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] sushi-port: serve response_format by instruction, visible
 queue, 503 on shutdown, DSV4.1 template + checks

Ported from sushi (https://github.com/beamivalice/sushi, MIT) at commit
3fc47d8a460970b1e86b24de1cab3b0f2067bc72:

- FIX 1 step A: response_format json_schema/json_object, guided_json/choice/regex and
  structured_outputs are no longer refused with HTTP 400 when the engine has no grammar mask
  (Info.structures false, the CUDA DeepSeek-V4.1 lanes engine): the schema instruction is
  appended to the leading system message before render (zig/src/server/schema_prompt.zig,
  after sushi src/server.zig response_format handling). guided_grammar (EBNF) stays refused.
  Not a decode mask: output follows the schema only as well as the model follows the prompt.
- Visible queue (sushi 1d16e45): [queue] log lines when a request waits for a lane and when it
  gets one; streamed requests get ': queued behind ...' SSE comments while waiting.
- Shutdown drain (sushi cb2525f): on SIGTERM/SIGINT queued and running replies end with 503
  (or a stream error event) instead of a short/empty 200; a closed scheduler answers 503.
- assets/dsv41: sushi's DeepSeek-V4.1 chat_template.jinja + 14 encoder-made cases, and
  zig build test-dsv41-template / tf-dsv41-template-cases to check them byte for byte with
  TensorFold's Jinja renderer.
- tools/blackfold: sushi's structured-output curl/jq tests adapted to a live serve.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md + LICENSES/MIT-sushi.txt attribution; docs/api.md updated.
