+**Native engines without a grammar mask** (`tensorfold-native` on the CUDA DeepSeek-V4.1 lanes engine, whose
+`Info.structures` is false) used to refuse these fields with HTTP 400. They now serve `response_format`
+(`json_schema`, `json_object`), `guided_json`, `guided_choice`, `guided_regex` and `structured_outputs` by
+instruction: the schema (or the JSON-only rule) is appended to the leading system message, or sent as a new system
+message, before the prompt renders (`zig/src/server/schema_prompt.zig`, ported from sushi, MIT,
+beamivalice/sushi @ 3fc47d8). Nothing masks the decode, so the reply follows the schema only as well as the model
+follows the instruction: validate it client-side. `guided_grammar` (EBNF) is still refused.
+
+## Queueing and shutdown (native server)
+
+When every lane is taken, a new request waits: the server logs `[queue] <id> queued behind R running and W waiting`
+and, once it gets a lane, `[queue] <id> got a lane after waiting Ns`. A streamed request that waits gets an SSE comment
+`: queued behind ...` at once and in place of each keepalive while it waits. On SIGTERM or SIGINT, replies still queued
+or decoding end with HTTP 503 (`the server is shutting down ...; retry it`), or an error event on a stream, instead of a
+short or empty 200. Ported from sushi commits 1d16e45 and cb2525f (MIT).
